msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/Privacy.php:387
msgid "Content from GitHub"
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/Privacy.php:388
msgid "Handbook pages can be imported and kept up to date from GitHub. These requests are made by this website's server to api.github.com, raw.githubusercontent.com and codeload.github.com. They name the repository and the files, and contain no data about the visitors of this site."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/Privacy.php:389
msgid "Searches without results"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: number of days the counts are kept.
#: src/Privacy/Privacy.php:392
#, php-format
msgid "When a search in a handbook finds no page, we count the search term so that the editors can see what is missing. We store the term in lower case, the handbook, the calendar week and whether the search came from the website or from an AI tool, nothing else: no user account, no IP address, no time of day and no cookie. Very short and very long terms are not stored. A term is stored as it was typed, so it can contain a name. Because nothing is tied to a person, these counts cannot be exported or erased for a person. They are deleted after %d days."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/Privacy.php:395
msgid "Progress through learning paths"
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/Privacy.php:396
