#: src/Setup/Settings.php:759
msgid "All four are on by default. Switching one off hides it: the column and the filter in the page list, the facet on a handbook's entry page, the badge on a page and on a card, and the field in the editor sidebar. An import stops reading its line as well."
msgstr ""

#: src/Setup/Settings.php:760
msgid "Nothing is deleted. The terms stay, the pages keep them, and switching one back on brings every assignment back exactly as it was. A bundle export carries all four either way, so moving a handbook to another site never loses what this site happens to hide."
msgstr ""

#: src/Setup/Settings.php:761
msgid "The handbook itself is not in this list and cannot be switched off: access hangs on it, and a page that belongs to no handbook is invisible on the front end."
msgstr ""

#: src/Setup/Settings.php:772
msgid "Use learning paths in this handbook installation"
msgstr ""

#: src/Setup/Settings.php:773
msgid "Off by default. A learning path is an ordered selection of pages that already exist in a handbook, for onboarding or for a piece of required reading. The pages stay where they are: a path only says which of them to read in which order."
msgstr ""

#: src/Setup/Settings.php:774
msgid "This first stage keeps no progress on the server. How far somebody has read is remembered in their browser and nowhere else, so nothing personal is stored, and the record is gone when they clear their browser data or change device. It is a guided path, not a record of attendance."
msgstr ""

#: src/Setup/Settings.php:775
msgid "Switching it off hides the learning paths and their menu entry. Nothing is deleted: the paths, their texts and their lesson lists stay, and switching it back on brings them back unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: src/Setup/Settings.php:785
msgid "Show \"Was this helpful?\" to logged-out visitors on public pages"
msgstr ""

#: src/Setup/Settings.php:786
msgid "Off by default. When on, anyone can vote on a public page. To keep it privacy-friendly, votes are not tied to a person: no cookie, no IP and nothing else personal is stored, so the same visitor can vote again after reloading. On internal pages only logged-in users vote, one vote each, regardless of this setting."
msgstr ""

#: src/Setup/Settings.php:800
msgid "Count searches that find nothing"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: number of days failed searches are kept.
#: src/Setup/Settings.php:804
#, php-format
msgid "On by default. Counts each search term that found no page, per handbook and calendar week, so editors see what readers look for and do not find. No user account, IP address, time of day or cookie is stored. Searches with filters selected are not counted. Counts are deleted after %d days, and when the plugin is deleted."
msgstr ""

#: src/Setup/Settings.php:836
msgid "How often WordPress pulls GitHub pages in the background, in batches. GitHub pages are always synced when saved and via Sync now, regardless of this setting. The background sync runs on WordPress cron, which fires on site visits."
msgstr ""

